# Pinned llvm-mingw release for the Windows build (maize-439).
#
# Format, and every reader honours it: lines whose first character is '#' are
# comments and blank lines are ignored. Of what remains, line 1 is the version
# and line 2 is the SHA256 of the release asset. Nothing else is parsed, so a
# third value needs a new file rather than a third line.
#
# This pin was chosen on maize-32 (resolved open question 5943): the newest
# llvm-mingw UCRT x86_64 release at the time, with no Microsoft Visual C++
# Redistributable dependency. Bump both lines together; recompute the hash with
# Get-FileHash on the downloaded asset.
#
# The asset name is derived, not stored: llvm-mingw-<version>-ucrt-x86_64.zip,
# from github.com/mstorsjo/llvm-mingw/releases/download/<version>/<asset>.
#
# A bump installs ALONGSIDE its predecessor, because the install path is keyed
# on this version, so a rollback costs nothing and two branches on different
# pins coexist. It also means a bump needs one bootstrap run per machine before
# any build finds the new compiler; see CLAUDE.md.
